"Build a decision-support tool for doctors (Meta Global AI Developer Hackathon, Theme 2 \"Build for Your World\", due Nov 4 2026 9:00 PM ET; must use Meta Model API models such as Muse Spark; synthetic or de-identified data only; decision support, not diagnosis). Components: (1) a knowledge graph encoding the latest clinical decision layer across medical specialties - symptoms, metrics/lab values, diagnoses and their sub-types, additional diagnostics needed to confirm and refine a diagnosis, tiered treatment plans (e.g. IBD: mesalamine, then steroids, then biologics such as Stelara or Remicade), metrics to monitor, diet, physiotherapy and other modalities, watch-outs and escalation triggers such as surgery - so the LLM is grounded and does not hallucinate; (2) an agentic layer (LangGraph or similar, using the hackathon LLM APIs) that answers by search and traversal over the graph so every output is auditable; (3) an audit layer that audits each session with built-in explainability; (4) an application layer where doctors chat with the agent alongside a canvas view of the knowledge-graph region used in the session, with a polished UI (design drafts to come); (5) an update layer: a silent background process that updates the graph, plus UI for a doctor to submit an update or link a new source which the agent then ingests, with versioning of the knowledge layer and comments. Example domain: gastroenterology / IBD, but the model must generalise to oncology, urology and other fields. Plan properly first; do not start building yet."
